From b6fa43242edb5de35cfe28822276f881302f6acb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 00:05:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] DolphinQt: XD Netplay launcher with one-click host and
 join

Add Tools > XD Netplay Launcher, a single dialog that walks a player from
a clean install to a GBA-link battle:

- Setup checklist with fix-it buttons: XD (USA) in the game list, Emerald
  ROM imported (raw .gba, header-validated, copied into the GBA user dir
  and wired to ports 2+3), bundled team saves, and the VS-mode memory
  card save. GBA input is an informational row pointing at the main
  Controllers settings.
- The GBA BIOS is invisible in the UI: no checklist row, no picker. The
  bundled open-source BIOS in Sys/GBA is sufficient and field-verified
  for the XD link, and any visible BIOS option would make users think
  they are missing something. The only BIOS behavior is a silent import:
  if a 16 KiB dump with the official SHA-1 sits next to the XD ISO, the
  auto-discovery scan adopts it and sets MAIN_GBA_BIOS_PATH.
- Auto-discovery: drop EMERALD.gba next to the XD ISO (or in a GBA/
  subfolder) and the launcher configures itself. The scan only runs
  while an item is unconfigured, only accepts ROMs whose internal title
  is POKEMON EMER so random GBA ROMs aren't grabbed, and never
  overwrites a valid configuration.
- One-click actions: solo boot (with a Practice vs dummy toggle for the
  port 3 auto-player), Host Battle, Join Battle via host code, and a
  shortcut to the public session browser. Hosting and joining force the
  known-good local config: pad/GBA/GBA SI devices, cheats on for the
  $XD OU Fixes code, fixed-delay netplay with a 5-frame buffer, no UPnP,
  traversal-server connections, and a default nickname.
- When a host presses Start in a Pokemon XD session, apply the same pad
  map forcing the Android build uses before the start request: host pad
  + host GBA + guest GBA, GBA slots 2/3 enabled, save sync, remote GBA
  hiding, and cheat code sync. Non-XD sessions are untouched.
